Scope and precedence
--------------------

1. PHG-authored software is licensed under the MIT License below. This covers
   phg/, scripts/, report/*.py, report/*.cjs, report/tests/, PHG-authored
   JavaScript, and software under extraction/protocols/**/code/, together with
   software configuration and build/dependency recipes. The software rule
   takes precedence over the non-code folder rule in item2.

2. PHG-authored report text, figures, derived data and extraction materials are
   licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
   This covers the PHG text/figures in index.html, report/prose.md, the narrative
   and figure outputs of report/phg_report.ipynb, PHG-authored material in data/,
   sources/, extraction/ (including portraits, question/statement banks,
   rubrics, item mappings and scientific protocols), provenance/,
   verification/, and repository documentation and CSV manifests. Notebook
   code cells remain MIT software. CC BY 4.0 legal text is provided in
   licenses/CC-BY-4.0.txt and at:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

   Suggested attribution: Josiah Chamberlain (2026), Persona–Human Geometry,
   https://github.com/J-Chamberlain/persona-human-geometry-report . Identify
   changes when adapting the material and retain relevant source citations.

3. These grants apply only to rights held by Josiah Chamberlain. Third-party
   terms and credits take precedence for third-party material: Plotly is MIT
   under report/vendor/PLOTLY_LICENSE; Lu et al.'s original released materials
   retain MIT terms; IPIP questionnaire items/scales/inventories remain public
   domain. The PHG table of published Petrov et al. values is a cited PHG
   arrangement: the original published values and original CSV are not
   relicensed by this notice. Raw human datasets, original model outputs,
   weights and any material not distributed here are not licensed here.
   See DATA_SOURCES.md for attribution and boundaries.

